---
import PublicPage from '../../components/public/PublicPage.astro';
---

<PublicPage
  label="Community"
  title="Community guidelines"
  description="How we keep itineraries useful, respectful, and trustworthy."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h2>Be useful, not promotional</h2>
    <p>
      Share the route you actually took. Explain timing, costs, and the parts that did not work. Do not
      use templates as an advert for a business or paste copied listicles.
    </p>

    <h2>Respect people and places</h2>
    <p>
      Ask before photographing people. Do not publish private information, exact home locations, or
      content that exposes vulnerable communities. Respect temples, homes, and protected areas.
    </p>

    <h2>Use licensed photos</h2>
    <p>
      Every photo needs a source, licence, credit, and meaningful alt text. Do not upload an image you
      found on another site unless you have permission.
    </p>

    <h2>Keep advice accurate</h2>
    <p>
      Flag uncertainty instead of presenting opening hours, prices, or safety conditions as fact. Update
      your template when you learn something important has changed.
    </p>

    <h2>No manipulation</h2>
    <p>
      Do not coordinate fake views, likes, saves, reviews, or qualified uses. Do not copy your own
      template through duplicate accounts. Competition manipulation is a suspension offence.
    </p>

    <h2>Moderation and appeals</h2>
    <p>
      Reports are private. Moderators may hide content, warn members, or suspend accounts. You will see
      a notification when a decision affects you. Ask for an administrator review if you believe a
      decision is wrong.
    </p>

    <h2>Report a problem</h2>
    <p>
      Use the Report link on a template, review, or profile. If the report concerns an urgent safety
      issue, contact <a href="mailto:safety@tosder.com">safety@tosder.com</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</PublicPage>

<style>
  .prose { max-width: 68ch; }
  h2 { margin: var(--space-5) 0 var(--space-2); font-size: var(--text-lg); font-weight: var(--weight-semibold); }
  p { color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: var(--text-sm); line-height: var(--leading-relaxed); }
  a { color: var(--color-text); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
</style>
